NAME
       unzip - list and unpack zip archives

SYNOPSIS
       unzip [-l] [-o] [-n] [-q] [-d DIRECTORY] ARCHIVE.zip [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
       unzip unpacks the files of a .zip archive (the format common on
       Windows) into the current directory, or into -d DIRECTORY. When a file
       already exists, unzip asks what to do unless -o or -n is given. It is
       in the unzip package, which is not installed by default.

OPTIONS
       -l     List the archive's contents without unpacking.

       -d DIRECTORY
              Unpack into DIRECTORY (created if needed).

       -o     Overwrite existing files without asking.

       -n     Never overwrite existing files.

       -q     Quiet.

EXAMPLES
           unzip -l /root/site.zip
           unzip /root/site.zip -d /var/www/html

SEE ALSO
       zip(1), tar(1), gzip(1)
